  <!-- COMPREHENSIVE ENGINEERING DOCUMENTATION -->
  <!-- ========================================================= -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <div class="rcc-footing-content">
      <h2>Complete RCC Isolated Pad & Sloped Footing Design Guide</h2>
      <p>
        An isolated pad footing (or spread footing) is a shallow foundation unit designed to distribute heavy concentrated loads from a single column safely onto the underlying soil stratum. Proper quantification of bottom reinforcement mesh cutting lengths, vertical development hooks, column starter dowels, concrete mix volume, and PCC blinding is crucial for site structural integrity and procurement efficiency as per <strong>IS 456:2000 (Cl. 34)</strong> and <strong>IS 2502:1963</strong>.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Mathematical Formulas for Footing Concrete Volume</h3>
      <p>
        Depending on structural engineering requirements, isolated footings are constructed either as uniform rectangular flat pads or economical trapezoidal (sloped) footings:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Flat Pad Footing Volume:</strong><br />
          <code>V = L × B × D</code><br />
          Where <em>L</em> = base length, <em>B</em> = base width, and <em>D</em> = total footing thickness.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Trapezoidal / Sloped Footing Volume (Prismoidal Formula):</strong><br />
          <code>V = V_base + V_trapezoid = (L × B × D₁) + [ (D - D₁) / 3 ] × [ A₁ + A₂ + √(A₁ × A₂) ]</code><br />
          Where <em>D₁</em> is the vertical edge depth, <em>A₁ = L × B</em> is bottom area, and <em>A₂ = a × b</em> is the top pedestal contact area.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2. Bar Bending Schedule (BBS) Cutting Length & Anchorage Hooks</h3>
      <p>
        As per <strong>IS 456 Cl. 26.4.2.2</strong>, footings must have a minimum clear cover of <strong>50 mm</strong> (or 75 mm when cast directly against unformed soil). To ensure full bending anchorage:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Bottom Mesh X-Bars (Spanning Length L):</strong><br />
          <code>Cutting Length = (L − 2 × Cover) + 2 × (D − 2 × Cover) − 2 × (2 × d)</code><br />
          Where <code>2 × (D − 2 × Cover)</code> represents the two vertical 90° end bend-ups, and <code>2 × (2 × d)</code> is the standard bend deduction for two 90° bends as prescribed by IS 2502.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bottom Mesh Y-Bars (Spanning Width B):</strong><br />
          <code>Cutting Length = (B − 2 × Cover) + 2 × (D − 2 × Cover) − 4 × d</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Column Starter Dowel Rebars:</strong><br />
          <code>Cutting Length = Development Lap (50d) + Embedment (D − Cover) + Foot Bend (300mm) − 2d</code><br />
          Dowels must project vertically by at least 50 times the bar diameter into the upper column and terminate with a minimum 300 mm 90° horizontal bend tied firmly to the footing mesh.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3. Standard Rebar Unit Weights & Commercial Bundles</h3>
      <p>
        Theoretical steel weight is computed using the standard mass formula <code>Unit Weight = d² / 162.2 kg/m</code>. Commercial TMT bars are delivered from rolling mills in standard <strong>12-meter (39.37 ft)</strong> lengths. The table below outlines standard factory bundle counts:
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-3">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-2 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">Rebar Diameter</th>
              <th class="p-2 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">Unit Wt (kg/m)</th>
              <th class="p-2 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">Unit Wt (lb/ft)</th>
              <th class="p-2 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">12m Rod Wt (kg)</th>
              <th class="p-2 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">Bars per Factory Bundle</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800">
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold">8 mm (#3)</td><td class="p-2">0.395 kg/m</td><td class="p-2">0.265 lb/ft</td><td class="p-2">4.74 kg</td><td class="p-2 font-semibold">10 Rods/Bundle</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold">10 mm</td><td class="p-2">0.617 kg/m</td><td class="p-2">0.414 lb/ft</td><td class="p-2">7.40 kg</td><td class="p-2 font-semibold">7 Rods/Bundle</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold">12 mm (#4)</td><td class="p-2">0.888 kg/m</td><td class="p-2">0.597 lb/ft</td><td class="p-2">10.66 kg</td><td class="p-2 font-semibold">5 Rods/Bundle</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold">16 mm (#5)</td><td class="p-2">1.578 kg/m</td><td class="p-2">1.060 lb/ft</td><td class="p-2">18.94 kg</td><td class="p-2 font-semibold">3 Rods/Bundle</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold">20 mm (#6)</td><td class="p-2">2.466 kg/m</td><td class="p-2">1.657 lb/ft</td><td class="p-2">29.60 kg</td><td class="p-2 font-semibold">2 Rods/Bundle</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold">25 mm (#8)</td><td class="p-2">3.853 kg/m</td><td class="p-2">2.589 lb/ft</td><td class="p-2">46.24 kg</td><td class="p-2 font-semibold">1 Rod/Bundle</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
